# Story: someone who lives in Emacs, where every ⌃⌥ + letter is a command, tells Arbor to leave the keys
# alone there. Emacs stays docked and the view still follows ⌘Tab; the shortcuts are back in any other app.
# Written by the executor swarm (F41); for the documenter to review.
# Reference: A61. Window ids start at 101; `open Emacs` has the bundle id com.example.emacs.
open Emacs
open Safari
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
focus 102
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+space on
# In Emacs: the menu's Shortcuts Off in "Emacs", or the command.
focus 101
pass-through
expect ok
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+space off
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+f off
# The one key that answers everywhere.
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+escape on
expect docked 101
# ⌘Tab to Safari: everything works again.
focus 102
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+space on
zoom
expect fills 102
expect hidden 101
# ⌘Tab back to Emacs, which is out of view: the view moves, as for any window, and the keys are Emacs's.
focus 101
expect visible 101
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+space off
# Changed their mind.
pass-through
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+space on
# A pause by hand inside a listed app, and back.
pass-through
toggle-pause
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+escape on
toggle-pause
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+space off
expect docked 101
